Enhancement: Support for TLS client certificates (mTLS)

The app can now connect to servers - or reverse proxies in front of them -
that require a TLS client certificate. A PKCS#12 (.p12/.pfx) file and its
password can be imported when adding an account or later in the account
editor. The certificate is stored in the shared keychain, so the File
Provider and the other extensions use it too, and it is only presented to
the server it was imported for. OAuth2/OpenID Connect logins to such
servers use an in-app browser session that can present the certificate.

